.TH uload "" "Administration"
.SH NAME
uload \- unload a device driver
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fB/etc/uload \fIfile\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
uload -- unload device driver
Usage:	/etc/uload file
Driver 'file' is usually found in directory '/drv'.
.HE
.B uload
removes from the running kernel the device driver contained in the
loadable driver image
.IR file ,
which was previously attached with
.BR load .
Driver
.I file
is usually found in directory
.BR /drv .
.PP
.B uload
reads
.I file
as an
.B l.out
executable and scans its symbol table for configuration-table symbols,
which the driver defines with a
.B con_
suffix (one per major device the driver implements).
For each one found, it reads the driver's configuration structure to
learn the major device number the driver occupies, and passes that
number to the
.BR suload ()
system call, which detaches the driver from the kernel's device
table.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B load
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B uload
complains and exits if
.I file
cannot be opened, is not a valid
.B l.out
image, or contains no configuration-table symbol.
For each configuration entry found, it also reports if the
.BR suload ()
call itself fails.
.SH NOTES
Only the superuser may unload a device driver.
